{{Quote|Could you arrange us a LAAT?''"<br />"''A larty? You'd be lucky.|[[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Clone Commander]] [[Varna]]|<ref name="Eye of the Beholder">{{StoryCite|story=The Eye of the Beholder|book=Stories of Jedi and Sith}}</ref>}}
The '''Low Altitude Assault Transport/infantry (LAAT/i)''', also referred to as the '''Republic Gunship''', '''Republic attack gunship''', '''Assault Gunship''', or '''LAATi''',<ref name="ESOV" /> and nicknamed a '''larty''',<ref name="Eye of the Beholder" /> was one of the several models in the [[Low Altitude Assault Transport]] line of [[starship]]s that mainly served as [[gunship]]s and [[troop transport]]s for the [[Grand Army of the Republic]] during the [[Clone Wars]]. Its role was to transport [[clone trooper]]s as well as offering air-to-ground and air-to-air support for the [[Galactic Republic]] against the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]]. The LAAT/i gunship saw extensive use in numerous battles and campaigns of the Clone Wars. During the [[Imperial Era]], the ships continued to see use by various factions, including both the [[Galactic Empire]] and [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]].

==Description==
{{Quote|Commander Cody, prepare the gunships for ground assault.|[[Jedi General]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], to [[Clone Commander]] [[Cody]]|<ref name="TCWfilm" />}}
[[File:Forward_Command_Center_AotC.png|thumb|left|250px|An LAAT/i lands Republic forces during the Battle of Geonosis]]
The Low Altitude Assault Transport/infantry [[gunship]] was a [[Republic Military|military]] [[repulsorcraft]]. Besides serving as an [[infantry]] transport, the LAAT/i gunship was also used to provide air-to-ground and air-to-air support for Republic forces. The front of the gunship had two double cockpit bubbles where the [[pilot]] and co-pilot/gunner sat in single file and could be sealed off from the rest of the gunship. A variety of equipment was located in the nose of the craft, including the flight computer and sensors.<ref name="Complete Vehicles" />

The LAAT/i gunship was armed with a varied mix of complementary weaponry which could unleash considerable firepower. A pair of dorsal [[mass-driver missile launcher]]s could fire a variety of ordance at up to hypersonic velocities and hit targets hiding over the horizon. These were fed by rear-mounted missile belts which utilized special frictionless material to load the weapons. Four [[composite-beam laser]] [[turret]]s provided for defense against airborne threats. Each turret had a wide field of rotation, but the composite-beam design allowed for precision aiming beyond a turret's physical rotation. Two of these were mounted in the wings and remotely controlled, while the other two extended out from the craft and were manually controlled by two gunners. Three anti-personnel [[laser cannon]] turrets&mdash;two mounted in the chin and one in the rear&mdash;were useful against infantry and other light ground targets. Each could vary the output on their laser shot to a maximum of five giga[[joule]]s. Lastly the gunship could carry eight light air-to-air rockets mounted beneath its wings.<ref name="Complete Vehicles" />

[[File:AirSupport-GRCCP.png|thumb|250px|left|LAAT/i's could provide covering fire for deployed troopers.]]
Beneath a surface layer of superficial armor plating, the LAAT/i was equipped with an inner layer of powered, superdispersive armoring which would spread the impact of enemy fire across the entire hull.<ref name="Complete Vehicles" /> It could also use its laser turrets to shoot down enemy missiles.<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref> When faced with overwhelming enemy fire, the gunship could close its [[Blast shield (gunship)|blast shields]].<ref name="TCWfilm" /> In a crash, the LAAT could deploy fire retardant and both the cockpit canopy and side doors could be explosively blown off to allow escape. Additional emergency equipment included medical packs and armor repair kits, collapsible repulsor stretches, inflatable decontamination tents, and a [[IM-6 Battlefield Medical Droid]].<ref name="Complete Vehicles" />

A LAAT/i gunship could carry a full [[platoon]] of thirty clone troopers in its main hold. The use of powerful [[Acceleration compensator|inertial compensators]] helped troopers to remain standing during their journey.<ref name="Complete Vehicles" /> It could also carry up to four speeder bikes.<ref name="Rise" /> These were deployed from the tail ramp, with the rear laser turret providing covering fire during deployment.<ref name="Complete Vehicles" />

The gunship's primary repulsor array was located along the bottom of the fuselage; additional altitude-control repulsors were mounted in the wings which, although not designed for aerodynamic lift, also helped to balance the craft. Designed specifically for maneuvering low in a planet's atmosphere, the LAAT/i was at an advantage when dogfighting [[starfighter]]s below the altitude of [[mountain]]s as the latter had to sacrifice their considerable speed advantage.<ref name="Complete Vehicles" /> While not originally designed for it, LAATs were later modified to allow for short trips in space.<ref name="ESOV" />

==History==
===Clone Wars===
{{Quote|Gunship come in. Hawk, we need an evac in the south tower.''"<br />"''Roger that, sir. We're coming.|[[Anakin Skywalker]] and [[clone trooper pilot]] [[Hawk]]|audio=HawkEvac-THE.flac|<ref name="The Hidden Enemy">{{TCW|The Hidden Enemy}}</ref>}}
<div style="float:right">[[File:Drop_Zone_EaW.png|thumb|220px|LAAT/i gunships deliver clone troopers to the battlefield at the Battle of Geonosis.]]</div>
LAAT/infantry gunships were first deployed during the [[First Battle of Geonosis]] in [[22 BBY]] as part of the [[Grand Army of the Republic]]. LAAT/i gunships attacked the [[Petranaki Arena]] and rescued [[Senator]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] and members of the [[Jedi Order]] from [[Count]] [[Dooku]]. LAAT/i gunships then saw action against the [[Separatist Droid Army]] alongside Low Altitude Assault Transport carriers and AT-TE walkers and proved instrumental in inflicting heavy damage on the Separatist droid forces. The Battle of Geonosis marked the beginning of the [[Clone Wars]], the first large-scale [[Galaxy|galactic]] wide conflict in a millennium.<ref name="Episode II" />

Republic gunships saw heavy use during the conflict, deploying troops to battlefronts like [[Battle of Teth|Teth]]<ref name="TCWfilm" /> and [[Battle of Umbara|Umbara]].<ref name="Darkness">{{TCW|Darkness on Umbara}}</ref> During the last days of the war in [[19 BBY]], LAAT/i gunships saw service on numerous worlds including [[Kashyyyk]] and [[Utapau]]. [[Jedi Master]]s [[Mace Windu]], [[Kit Fisto]], [[Agen Kolar]], and [[Saesee Tiin]] traveled on an LAAT/i gunship to confront [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine]], who was the [[Sith Lord]] Darth Sidious. Their failed attempt to arrest Palpatine led to the initiation of [[Order 66]] and the transformation of the [[Galactic Republic]] into the [[Galactic Empire]]<ref name="Episode III" />, which saw 2 of them being utilized by the [[Coruscant Guard]] to chase [[Kelleran Beq]] and [[Din Grogu]] who had stolen a [[BARC speeder]] from the [[501st Legion]] during their attack on the Jedi Temple, though one of them was destroyed by a [[Hovertrain]] at the [[Manarai range]].<ref name="Chapter 20">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 20: The Foundling}} {{Flash}}</ref>

===Imperial Era===
[[File:Databank-ImpEraGunship.png|thumb|left|300px|An LAAT/i in service to the Empire]]
Following the formation of the Galactic Empire, the LAAT/is were absorbed into the [[Imperial Navy]].<ref name="Tarkin" /> Many were given the typical grey coloration of the [[Imperial Military]],<ref name="Point of No Return">{{TBB|Point of No Return (The Bad Batch)}}</ref> although it was not impossible for an Imperial-deployed LAAT/i to retain a white design with accents of another color, such as blue.<ref name="Insider153">{{InsiderCite|153|Tarkin Revealed}}</ref> Under Imperial service, the gunships continued to transport and deploy troopers into battle in addition to taking prisoners, such as [[Cham Syndulla]], his [[Eleni Syndulla|wife]], and several resistance fighters on [[Ryloth]].<ref name="Deal">{{TBB|Devil's Deal}}</ref> The LAAT/is could also be used in dogfights and strafing runs, such as when several intercepted [[Clone Force 99]] during an effort to recapture an escaped [[Zillo Beast]] on [[Silla]]<ref name="Metamorphosis">{{TBB|Metamorphosis (episode)}}</ref> or when destroying fishing ships and skiffs on [[Pabu]] to prevent [[Omega]]'s escape during the [[raid on Pabu]].<ref name="Point of No Return" /> 

Several LAAT/is were present at an Imperial [[Cassaro shipyard|shipyard]] on [[Cassaro]] and were deployed in an attempt to prevent [[C-21 Highsinger]], [[Asajj Ventress]], and [[Lyco Strata]] from [[Heist at Cassaro shipyard|stealing]] an [[Imperial shield relay unit]].<ref name="Friends">{{TOTU|Friends}}</ref> The [[Wookiee]]s of the [[Kashyyyk resistance]] used LAAT/is leftover from the Clone Wars in defending their [[homeworld]] from [[Occupation of Kashyyyk|Imperial subjugation]]; these particular gunships had their wings and missile launchers repainted yellow.<ref name="Fallen Order" /> By the following years leading up to the [[Galactic Civil War]],<ref name="Call to Action">{{Rebels|Call to Action}}</ref> the Empire had largely replaced the LAAT/i with the cheaper [[Imperial Dropship Transport]]<ref name="Forged">''[[Forged in Battle]]''</ref> and smaller [[LAAT/le patrol gunship]].<ref name="Call to Action">{{Rebels|Call to Action}}</ref>

[[File:WookieeLAAT.png|thumb|right|300px|An LAAT/i used by the Kashyyyk resistance]]
Rebel factions such as the Kashyyyk resistance, the [[Partisans]],<ref name="Fallen Order" /> and [[Hidden Path]] made use of the LAAT/i, with the Hidden Path making use of several on the holy [[moon]] of [[Jedha]].<ref name="Survivor" /> Thereafter during the Galactic Civil War, some LAAT/is were used by the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] against Imperial forces.<ref name="Star Wars: Commander" /> The [[Skakoan]] revolutionary [[Jul Tambor]] also got his hands on at least three LAATs.<ref name="Vader 31" /> By [[5 ABY]],<ref name="Life Debt date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''[[Aftermath: Life Debt]]'' to [[5 ABY]].</ref> a more advanced variant of the aging LAAT/i, the [[low-altitude Imperial transport]], was in use; one of which was used by the [[Imperial territory G5-623|remnant of the Galactic Empire]] led by [[Grand Moff]] [[Lozen Tolruck]] on Kashyyyk.<ref name="ALD">''[[Aftermath: Life Debt]]''</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The ship first appeared in the [[2002]] film [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']], where it was referred to as the "Jedi attack helicopter" in pre-production. ''[[Star Wars]]'' creator [[George Lucas]] used news footage of helicopter-based infantry deployment as an inspiration for the design. The cockpit configuration in particular was inspired by the Russian [[Wikipedia:Mil Mi-24|Mil Mi-24 "Hind"]] attack helicopter.<ref name="SW:DB">{{DB|vehicle|republicgunship|Republic attack gunship}}</ref>

